  "problem": "A company is selling a new product on three e-commerce platforms, platform $1,$ platform $2,$ and platform $3.$\n\n- $56%$ of customers bought the product on platform $1,$ and $96%$ of those customers were satisfied with the product.\n\n- $14%$ of customers bought the product on platform $2,$ and $80%$ of those customers were satisfied with the product.\n\n- $30%$ of customers bought the product on platform $3,$ and $90%$ of those customers were satisfied with the product.\n\nIf $45%$ of all customers are teenagers and $92%$ of teenage customers are satisfied with the product, what is the probability that a randomly chosen satisfied customer is a teenager? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
